WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.180
Football season is upon us, and apparently,
this means it's time to talk politics.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.910
I wish we could separate sports and politics,
or pretty much everything and politics, but

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:18.750
somehow politics has infected every facet
of American life.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:24.080
Inserting politics into virtually everything
we consume is a really bad sign as to what

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.759
direction this country is heading.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:30.599
That isn't to deny the feelings of the players
who take the knee, but it is to acknowledge

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:33.670
why people watch sports in the first place.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:38.559
People turn to sports, video games, and other
entertainment to escape politics and the cold

00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:40.149
hard realities of life.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:44.649
Now, it seems everywhere you turn, politics
has reared its ugly head.

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:48.019
If you don't take a side and scream about
it, or at least tweet about it, then you'll

00:00:48.019 --> 00:00:53.859
be tossed in as racist or anti American, depending
on who is leveling the charge.

00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:59.199
When our momentary escapes from reality...like
sports... are taken away from us in exchange

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:04.280
for more political fighting, we should all
take a step back and asses what's really going

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.280
on here.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.730
OK, so let's start with Trump.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:11.720
Trump kicked this whole controversy off on
Friday night at a speech in Alabama where

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:17.350
he said that NFL owners should get rid of
players who don't stand for the national anthem,

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:23.140
saying "Get that son of a bitch off the field
right now, he's fired.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.980
He's fired!"

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.340
Now let me be crystal clear here: calling
a football player, or any other citizen a

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:35.140
son of a bitch under any circumstances is
not the type of language I'd like to hear

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.310
from the highest office in the land.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.580
As a free speech supporter, I do have major
concerns about the chill factor around free

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.250
speech when the president makes comments like
this.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:49.760
Personally, I'd much rather have a president
who could share his own personal beliefs on

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.940
a matter, while still affirming the right
of every citizen to protest, while and also

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.810
acknowledging private companies can tend to
their employees however they see fit.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.850
That's how this exchange is supposed to work
in a free society.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.200
The president can say whatever he wants, the
football players can do whatever they want,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:14.189
the teams can respond as they see fit -- and
you, too, can use your voice to share your

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:16.069
feelings on it all.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:21.019
So again, to be clear here, even if Trump
isn't saying or tweeting statements just as

00:02:21.019 --> 00:02:25.859
I'd like him to, he has the exact same right
to free speech the rest of us have.

00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:31.590
Now, if he tried to instruct federal agencies
to punish players or football teams teams

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:36.849
for exercising their right to free speech,
we would have an illegal act and an impeachable

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:37.849
offense.

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:42.700
As far as I can see, he didn't do that, though
he did intentionally inflame the situation

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:48.439
by getting as close to seeming to use government
authority to silence people without quite

00:02:48.439 --> 00:02:50.310
doing so.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:54.829
Understanding that Trump said something, but
didn't sign an executive action on it is an

00:02:54.829 --> 00:03:00.430
important distinction though, because words
are not action, even when those words are

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:03.389
uttered by the president of the United States.

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:08.349
And it's worth mentioning that these protests
started under Obama, so while Trump has added

00:03:08.349 --> 00:03:13.230
fuel to the fire, the seeds of these protests
had already been planted.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.400
Now onto the players.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.609
It is 100% within the players right to exercise
their free speech as they say fit.

00:03:19.609 --> 00:03:23.209
While I personally would never kneel during
the national anthem, it is completely within

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:24.810
their right to do so.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:29.371
And for those of you who think kneeling during
the anthem is unamerican, or not the player's

00:03:29.371 --> 00:03:33.439
right to do so, imagine for a moment what
kind of country you'd be living in if people

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:35.799
couldn't protest peacefully.

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:40.680
You may think that these players are misguided
or mistaken, but imagine the society we'd

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:45.890
be living in if the government could force
people to stand for our national anthem.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:50.169
What else could the government force us to
do against our will once we've given it that

00:03:50.169 --> 00:03:51.459
power?

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:55.269
Of course, the players exercising their right
to free speech must understand that their

00:03:55.269 --> 00:03:58.300
actions might have consequences as well.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:03.239
This is the implicit exchange we all must
make to live in a truly free society.

00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:07.989
NFL teams can fine or suspend players as they
see fit, and nobody has an inherent right

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:09.099
to play in the NFL.

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:13.680
By the way, nobody has in inherent right to
work at Google either, but I didn't see many

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.590
of the people who are standing up the players
right now also stand up for fired Google engineer

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:23.509
James Damore when he voiced his opinion on
Google's diversity program.

00:04:23.509 --> 00:04:27.819
Interestingly, Damore was fired for doing
exactly what the company had asked him to

00:04:27.819 --> 00:04:32.080
do....attend a diversity course and then share
his opinions on it.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.979
So to recap, Trump can say what he wants as
long as he doesn't use his government influence

00:04:37.979 --> 00:04:43.830
to silence people, players can do what they
want knowing there could be repercussions,

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:48.180
and teams can deal with players however they
see fit.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.919
So now onto you, the public.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:56.120
If football fans don't want to buy tickets
or watch the games because of the protests,

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:01.669
well at the end of the day, even the great
American pastime of football is just a business

00:05:01.669 --> 00:05:07.440
-- owners and management have the right and
the duty to do what's best for their business.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.030
If nobody is buying tickets, watching on the
games on TV, or buying merchandise, then there

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:15.750
will be nobody to see the protests in the
first place.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.210
This is the beauty of capitalism.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:23.169
Everyone from the president to the owners
to the players to the fans all have the ability

00:05:23.169 --> 00:05:27.020
to exercise their speech as they see fit.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.419
And if their speech isn't enough to make a
dent in a cause they believe in then they

00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:35.159
can still support a cause, or not, with their
hard earned dollars.

00:05:35.159 --> 00:05:38.830
This is freedom actually working right in
front of our eyes and virtually all of the

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.830
media is making it seem like this is the end
of civilization.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:47.509
If you stand with Colin Kapernick and the
other players, then feel free to boycott the

00:05:47.509 --> 00:05:48.509
NFL.

00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:52.879
If you don't like the American flag being
disrespected by the players, then boycott

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:54.050
the NFL.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:58.879
I'd rather just watch some football, or in
my case basketball, but you have the capacity

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:02.169
and right to do whatever you want.

00:06:02.169 --> 00:06:10.379
To be very clear: I 100% stand by these players
doing whatever to protest or not if that's

00:06:10.379 --> 00:06:12.660
what their conscience tells them to do.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:17.039
I also stand by their employers to do what
they feel is right for their business even

00:06:17.039 --> 00:06:21.569
if I don't agree with it, and I do not want
the government to pass any law which would

00:06:21.569 --> 00:06:25.750
impeded on the rights of the players or any
sports organization.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:31.860
This position doesn't deny anyone's grievances
or feelings, it actually maximizes personal

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:35.939
responsibility which is the cornerstone of
a free society.

00:06:35.939 --> 00:06:39.879
Like I said before, while I'd love politics
out of sports and sports out of politics,

00:06:39.879 --> 00:06:44.320
it now seems that our president and our media
isn't going to let this seperation happen.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:48.439
I basically never watch Sports Center anymore
because it's an endless blotter of crime stories

00:06:48.439 --> 00:06:52.129
and politics with game highlights tossed in
for good measure.

00:06:52.129 --> 00:06:57.159
What those of us who want to respect our fellow
citizens and the law can do, is to discuss

00:06:57.159 --> 00:07:01.639
the situtaion within the framework of what
it truly means to be free.

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:05.599
Nobody has been fired because of their speech,
athough Kapernick does remains a free agent...which

00:07:05.599 --> 00:07:07.909
goes back to that consequences thing...

00:07:07.909 --> 00:07:13.910
no law has been passed to actually silence
anyone, and we all have an equal chance for

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.879
our opinion to be heard.

00:07:15.879 --> 00:07:20.639
While many would point only to the evils of
our political system, this story is actually

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:23.330
showing the strength of our democracy.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.990
Don't like Trump's statements?

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:26.169
Don't vote for him.

00:07:26.169 --> 00:07:28.380
Don't like the players who sat for the anthem?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.740
Don't buy their jersey.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:31.319
Sick of the whole damn thing?

00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:35.439
Find something better to do than drink beer
and watch football on Sundays.

00:07:35.439 --> 00:07:39.639
All of the discussion and debate around kneeling
for the anthem and honoring the country is

00:07:39.639 --> 00:07:43.840
healthy as long as it doesn't turn into violence
and tyranny.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:49.139
Calmer heads can win this game as long as
we stand for the principles of free speech

00:07:49.139 --> 00:07:53.000
and the right to a peaceful protest, even
when we don't want to.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:57.719
The second we set aside our principles we're
just picking a political team and rooting

00:07:57.719 --> 00:08:00.669
for our side as if it were a football game.

00:08:00.669 --> 00:08:04.550
For now, though, I'll pass on picking a team
and remain a free agent in the marketplace

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:04.620
of ideas.

